# servers.txt.lab — fleet-scan template for the php2shell lab
#
# Do NOT edit this file. Generate a ready-to-use servers.txt with:
#   ./make-servers-txt.sh          (host side, after `vagrant up`)
#
# The generated lines look like:
#   vagrant@127.0.0.1 -p 2222 -i /abs/path/.vagrant/machines/default/virtualbox/private_key -o IdentitiesOnly=yes
#
# When you move to the REAL Debian/Ubuntu boxes on your closed LAN, create a
# servers.txt with one ssh destination per line, e.g.:
#   ops@web-01
#   ops@192.168.10.20 -p 2222
#   ubuntu@db-01 -i ~/.ssh/lab_key
#
# Scan them:      bash php2shell-check.sh --servers servers.txt
# Exact verdicts: ssh <target> 'sudo bash -s' < php2shell-check.sh --once
#                 (fleet probes are deliberately conservative; backport-proof
#                  verdicts need the checker run on the target itself)
